            <div xml:id="d791">

                <pb facs="0742" n="738" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/13614: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-outside-research" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-03">undated</date>].<lb/>[Received August 3—11:29
                        a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Hankow raided by 18 Japanese bombers this morning. Bombs dropped in the vicinity
                    airfield.</p>
                <p>Chinese customs vessel bombed and sunk by Japanese planes yesterday 36 miles
                    below Hankow. Customs river officer J. T. C. Crawley, British, and two members
                    of Chinese crew were killed and several wounded. His Majesty’s ship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gnat</hi> proceeded scene early this morning.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Embassy and Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
